          #TopAsASymmetricMonoidalCategory.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              between them, regarded as enriched in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+spaces"} discrete topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              of sets. The
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              isomorphism are the evident (almost unnoticable but nevertheless nontrivial) canonical identifications.
            %p
              Similarly the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#kTop"}> def.
              ) becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              the corresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"} cor.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ProductTopologicalSpace"}> exmpl.
              ). The underlying functions of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              isomorphisms are just those of the underlying sets, as above.
            %p
              Symmetric monoidal categories, such as these, for which the tensor product is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+monoidal+categories"} Cartesian monoidal categories
            %p
              Both examples are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+categories"} closed monoidal categories
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#MappingTopologicalSpaceIsExponentialObject"}> prop.
              ).
          #PointedTopologicalSpacesWithSmashIsSymmetricMonoidalCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#SmashProductOfPointedObjects"}> def.
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ≔
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \wedge Y \coloneqq \frac{X\times Y}{X\vee Y}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
              the pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
            %p
              The components of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              are those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              as in example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopAsASymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topological+spaces"} quotient topological spaces
              which appear in the definition of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+spaces"} compactly generated spaces
              (but not for general pointed topological spaces) by
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#SmashProductInTopcgIsAssociative"} this prop.
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
              is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              the pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(-,-)_\ast
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#PointedMappingSpace"}> exmpl.
              )
          #ExampleAbelianGroupsOfMonoidalCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+spaces"} discrete topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              with tensor product the actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}}
              and with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              the additive group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              isomorphism are the evident ones coming from the underlying sets, as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopAsASymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
            %p
              This is a
              %span.newWikiWord
                closd monoidal cagory
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/closd+monoidal+cagory"} ?
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(A,B)
              being the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{Ab}(A,B)
              equipped with the pointwise group structure for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_1, \phi_2 \in Hom_{Ab}(A,B)
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi_1 + \phi_2)(a) \coloneqq \phi_1(a) + \phi_2(b) \; \in B
            %p
              This is the archetypical case that motivates the notation “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              ” for the pairing operation in a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          #SymmetricMonoidalCategoryOfChainComplexes.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
            %p
              In this case the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              has a genuinely non-trivial aspect to it, beyond just the swapping of coordinates as in examples
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopAsASymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedTopologicalSpacesWithSmashIsSymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              and def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExampleAbelianGroupsOfMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in Ch_\bullet
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X \otimes Y)_n
                    \=
                    \\underset{n_1 + n_2 = n}{\otimes}
                    X_{n_1} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} X_{n_2}
            %p
              and in these components the braiding isomorphism is that of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %p This is a first shadow of the graded-commutativity that also exhibited by spectra.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey 99, prop. 4.2.13
          %h5#AlgebrasAndModules Algebras and modules
          #MonoidsInMonoidalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Given a (pointed)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \;\colon\; 1 \longrightarrow A
                  (called the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \;\colon\; A \otimes A \longrightarrow A
                  (called the
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %em product
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"}> associativity
                  ) the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %munderover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi a
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi μ
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi μ
                                      %mo ⊗
                                      %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi μ
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        (A\otimes A) \otimes A
                        \&amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{a_{A,A,A}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes (A \otimes A)
                        \&amp;\overset{A \otimes \mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes A
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{\mu \otimes A}}\downarrow
                        \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                        \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mu}}
                        \\\
                        A \otimes A
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        \&amp;\overset{\mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A
                        }
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  is the associator isomorphism of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li#UnitalityMonoid
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"}> unitality
                  ) the following
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi id
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi e
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi ℓ
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi r
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        1 \otimes A
                        \&amp;\overset{e \otimes id}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes A
                        \&amp;\overset{id \otimes e}{\longleftarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes 1
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\ell}}\searrow
                        \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mu}} &amp;
                        \&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{r}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; A
                        }
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  are the left and right unitor isomorphisms of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Moreover, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes , 1)
              has the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1, B)
              with symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mu, e)
              as above is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+category"} commutative monoid in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1, B)
              if in addition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  (commutativity) the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %munderover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi τ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
