                  \\,.
          %p
            The operation of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of this situation where functions are replaced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %a{:href => "#OnPreExcisiveFunctors"} below
            we find the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            as the Day convolution of topologically enriched functors over the monoidal category of finite pointed CW-complexes, or over sufficiently rich subcategories thereof.
          #TopologicalDayConvolutionProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
