          .proof
            %h6#proof_16 Proof
            %p
              This is an immediate corollary of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayMonoidsAreLaxMonoidalFunctorsOnTheSite"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalFunctorComp"}
          %h4#SModules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            \-Modules
          %p We give a unified discussion of the categories of
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            %li
              %p
                pre-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
          %p
            (all in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
            with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            monoidal structures on
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+categories"} enriched functor categories
            over restrictions to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
            sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
            of the canonical representative of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            as a pre-excisive functor on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{fin}
          %p
            This approach is due to (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> Mandell-May-Schwede-Shipley 00
            ) following (
            %a{:href => "HoveyShipleySmith00"}> Hovey-Shipley-Smith 00
            ).
          %h5#OnPreExcisiveFunctors Pre-Excisive functors
          %p
            We consider an almost tautological construction of a pointed topologically enriched category equipped with a closed symmetric monoidal product: the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-excisive+functors"} pre-excisive functors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            on sequential spectra. However from inspection of this failure we see that there are categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+spectra"} structured spectra
            “in between” those of all pre-excisive functors and plain sequential spectra, notably the categories of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            that we are after.
          %p
            %strong Literature
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, Part I and Part III
            )
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #FinitePointedCWComplexes.num_defn
            %h6#definition_16 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi fin
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi cg
                        %mo ,
                        %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota_{fin}\;\colon\; Top^{\ast/}_{cg,fin} \hookrightarrow Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#Top"}> def.
              ) on those that admit the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complex"} finite CW-complex
              (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopologicalCellComplex"}> def.
              ) with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of cells).
            %p
              We say that the pointed topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedTopologicalFunctorCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Exc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi cg
                        %mo ,
                        %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Exc(Top_{cg})
                    \\coloneqq
                    [Top^{\ast/}_{cg,fin}, Top^{\ast/}_{cg}]
            %p
              is the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-excisive+functors"} pre-excisive functors
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P"} Part P
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#PreExcisiveFunctors"} this example
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi exc
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi cg
                        %mo ,
                        %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{exc}
                    \\coloneqq
                    y(S^0)
                    \\coloneqq
                    Top^{\ast/}_{cg,fin}(S^0,-)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} functor co-represented
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi fin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{fin}
              itself:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi exc
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi fin
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{exc} = \iota_{fin}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    K \mapsto K
                    \\,.
            %p
              We call this the standard incarnation of the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              as a pre-excisive functor.
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayConvolutionYieldsMonoidalCategoryStructure"}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              induces the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi Exc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Day
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi exc
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    Exc(Top_{cg})
                    ,\;
                    \\wedge \coloneqq \otimes_{Day}
                    ,\;
                    \\mathbb{S}_{exc}
                    \\right)
            %p with
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝕊
                            %mi exc
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{exc}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution+product"} Day convolution product
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi Day
