          #DiagramSpectraGiveSymmetricAndOrthogonalSpectra.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_19 Proposition
            %p
              Definitions
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricSpectrum"}
              and
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalSpectrum"}
              are indeed equivalent to def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SsymModuleSymmetricSpectra"}
            %p
              orthogonal spectra are euqivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              over the incarnation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi orth
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{orth}
              of the sphere spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi orth
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    OrthSpec(Top_{cg})
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{S}_{orth} Mod
            %p
              and symmetric spectra sre equivalently the module objects over the incarnation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi sym
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{sym}
              of the sphere spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SymSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi sym
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SymSpec(Top_{cg})
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{S}_{sym} Mod
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HoveyShipleySmith00"}> Hovey-Shipley-Smith 00, prop. 2.2.1
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_21 Proof
            %p We discuss this for symmetric spectra. The proof for orthogonal spectra is of the same form.
            %p
              First of all, by example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoendGivesQuotientByDiagonalGroupAction"}
              an object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Sym, Top^{\ast/}_{cg}]
              is equivalently a “symmetric sequence”, namely a sequence of pointed topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_k
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(k)
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
            %p
              By corollary
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DayConvolutionViaNaturalIsosInvolvingExternalTensorAndTensor"}
              and lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FSPStructuredSphereSpectra"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi sym
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{sym}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+object"} module object
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi sym
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Day
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{sym} \otimes_{Day} X \longrightarrow X
            %p
              is equivalently (as a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+with+smash+products"} functor with smash products
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n_1} \wedge X_{n_2} \longrightarrow X_{n_1 + n_2}
            %p
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sym
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Sym
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym \times Sym
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_1, n_2 \in \mathbb{N}
              and that it is
              = succeed "-equivariant." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma(n_1) \times \Sigma(n_2)
            %p
              Hence it only remains to see that these natural transformations are uniquely fixed once the one for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_1 = 1
              is given. To that end, observe that lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FSPStructuredSphereSpectra"}
              says that in the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
              (exhibiting the action property on the level of functors with smash product, where we are notationally suppressing the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associators"} associators
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 3
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 3
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 3
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 3
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n_1}\wedge S^{n_2} \wedge X_{n_3}
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    S^{n_1} \wedge X_{n_2 + n_3}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    S^{n_1+ n_2} \wedge X_{n_3}
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    X_{n_1 + n_2 + n_3}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This says exactly that the action of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n_1 + n_2}
              has to be the composite of the actions of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n_2}
              followed by that of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n_1}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              Finally, the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              on both sides of the equivalence are just so as to preserve precisely this structure, hence they conincide under this identification.
          #SmashProductOfSymmetricSpectra.num_defn
