                    \\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
            %p
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeStructuredSpectrum"}
              have component spaces that admit the structure of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
          .proof
            %h6#proof_32 Proof
            %p
              We consider the case of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
              works verbatim the same, and the case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
              is tivial.
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitFormOfFreeSpectra"}
              we have to show that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \geq n \in \mathbb{N}
              the topological spaces of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mrow
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O(q)_+ \wedge_{O(q-n)} S^{q-n}
                    \\;\;
                    \\in Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
            %p admit the structure of CW-complexes.
            %p
              To that end, use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{q-n} \simeq D^{q-n}/\partial D^{q-n}
            %p
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
              away from the basepoint and hence such that the action of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(q-n)
              induces a smooth action on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
