              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
              ) whose weak equivalences and fibrations are those morphisms which induce on all component spaces weak equivalences or fibrations, respectively, in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
