          .proof
            %h6#proof_38 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModulesForDayConvolutionAsEnrichedFunctors"}
              all four categories are equivalently categories of pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Free
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
                    \\simeq
                    [ \mathbb{S}_{dia} Free_{dia}Mod, Top^{\ast/}_{cg} ]
            %p
              and hence the existence of the model structures with componentwise weak equivalences and fibrations is a special case of the general existence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+enriched+functors"} projective model structure on enriched functors
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopologicalFunctors"}> thm.
              ).
            %p
              The three restriction functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi dia
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dia^\ast
              each have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dia
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dia_!
              by topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
              (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalLeftKanExtensionBCoend"}
            %p
              Moreover, the three right adjoint restriction functors are along inclusions of objects, hence evidently preserve componentwise weak equivalences and fibrations. Hence these are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunctions"} Quillen adjunctions
          #GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_27 Definition
            %p Recall the sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
