          #PushoutProductWithRespectToSmashTensoringSatisfiesEnrichedModelCategoryAxioms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_27 Proposition
            %p
              The operations of forming pushout products and pullback powering with respect to smash tensoring in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductWithRespectToSmashTensoring"}
              is compatible with the strict model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod_{strict}
              on structured spectra from theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              and with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ClassicalModelStructureOnCompactlyGeneratedTopologicalSpaces"}> thm.
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelStructureOnSliceCategory"} prop.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Cof
                              %mi strict
                            %mo □
                            %msub
                              %mi Cof
                              %mi cl
