          %h5#monoidal_model_structure Monoidal model structure
          %p
            We now combine the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
          %p
            Given a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            that is equipped both with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            and of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}> def.
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            exists to equip also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
            with the structure of a monoidal category. If so, then one may furthermore ask if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow Ho(\mathcal{C})
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
          %p
            The axioms on a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
            below) are such as to ensure that this is the case.
          %p
            A key consequence is that, via prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsPreservedByLaxMonoidalFunctor"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            carries monoids to monoids. Applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable model category
            of spectra established below, this gives that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+ring+spectra"} structured ring spectra
            indeed represent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            in the homotopy category. (In fact much more is true, but requires further proof: there is also a model structure on monoids in the model structure of spectra, and with respect to that the structured ring spectra represent
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-infinity+rings"} A-infinity rings
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+rings"} E-infinity rings
          #MonoidalModelCategory.num_defn
