          %p Observe some immediate consequences of these axioms:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              Since a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes (-) \simeq (-) \otimes X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and hence preserves all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              (which is the colimit over the empty diagram).
            %p
              If follows that the tensor-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              implies that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a cofibrant object, then the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \otimes (-)
              preserves cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations, since
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \Box_\otimes (\emptyset \to X)
                    \\simeq
                    f \otimes X
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              happens to be cofibrant, then the unit axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              is already implied by the pushout-product axiom. This is because then we have a lift in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ∅
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Q
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\emptyset &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Q 1
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\in Cof}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;\nearrow&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p_1}}_{\mathrlap{\in W}}
                    \\\
                    1 &amp;=&amp; 1
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This lift is a weak equivalence by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}> def.
              ). Since it is hence a weak equivalence between cofibrant objects, it is preserved by the left Quillen functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes X
              (for any cofibrant
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"} Ken Brown's lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#KenBrownLemma"}> prop.
              ). Hence now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1 \otimes X
              is a weak equivalence by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
            %p
              Since for all the categories of spectra that we are interested in here the tensor unit is always cofibrant (it is always a version of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi dia
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_{dia}
              of the cofibrant pointed space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionSpectrumStructuredStrictQuillenAdjunction"}
          #MonoidalStructureOnHomotopyCategoryOfMonoidalModelCategory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_31 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, I)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes^L
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctors"}> def.
              ) of the tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              exsists and makes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> def.
              ) into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ho(\mathcal{C}), \otimes^L, \gamma(1))
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\colon \mathcal{C}_c\to Ho(\mathcal{C})
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cofibrant+objects"} category of cofibrant objects
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}> def.
              ) carries the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    (Ho(\mathcal{C}), \otimes^L , \gamma(1))
                    \\,.
          %p
            The first statement is also for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Hovey99"}> Hovey 99, theorem 4.3.2
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_45 Proof
            %p
              For the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LeftAndRightDerivedFunctorsOnModelCategories"}> def.
              ) of the tensor product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\otimes
                    \\;
                    \\mathcal{C}\times \mathcal{C}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathcal{C}
            %p to exist, it is sufficient that its restriction to the subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi c
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C})_c
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathcal{C}_c \times \mathcal{C}_c
            %p
              of cofibrant objects preserves acyclic cofibrations (by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ken+Brown%27s+lemma"} Ken Brown's lemma
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#KenBrownLemma"} here
            %p
              Every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi c
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{c}\times \mathcal{C}_{c}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OppositeAndProductOfPointedTopologicallyEnrichedCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f,g)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (c_1, d_1)
                    \\overset{(id_{c_1},g)}{\longrightarrow}
                    (c_1,d_2)
                    \\overset{(f,id_{c_2})}{\longrightarrow}
                    (c_2,d_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              (with respect to tensor product) with the initial morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ast \to c_1)
              is equivalently the tensor product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\ast \to c_1) \Box_{\otimes} g
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    id_{c_1} \otimes g
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \Box_{\otimes} (\ast \to c_2)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    f \otimes id_{c_2}
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalModelCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              preserves acyclic cofibrations. (This is why one speaks of a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Hovey99"} Hovey 99, prop. 4.3.1
            %p
              Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes^L
              exists.
            %p
              By the same decomposition and using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of a category (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfACategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}> def.
              ) one finds that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              any two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+weak+equivalences"} categories with weak equivalences
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}> def.
              ) then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              is the product category of their localizations:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
