            %p
              The top square stabilizes to the actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableHomotopyCategoryIsIndeedStabilizationOfClassicalHomotopyCategory"}> thm.
              ). On the other hand, the top square does not reflect the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
              (by remark
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RestrictionsOfExcisiveSphere"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi dia
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi dia
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_{dia} = dia_! \Sigma^\infty
              does, in that it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} strong monoidal Quillen adjunction
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalQuillenAdjunction"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionSpectrumStructuredStrictQuillenAdjunction"}
            %p
              Hence to obtain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable model category
              which is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              with respect to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (seq_! \dashv seq^\ast)
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenEquivalence"}> def.
              )
          %p
            This we now turn to in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#MonoidalStableModelStructure"} The stable model structure on structured spectra
          %h4#MonoidalStableModelStructure The stable model structure on structured spectra
          #OrthogonalSpectraStableModelStructure.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OrthSpec(Top_{cg})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
              carries a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              structure (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
              ) where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the weak equivalences
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi stable
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{stable}
                  are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalences"} stable weak homotopy equivalences
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
              %li
                %p
                  the cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Cof
                          %mi stable
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof_{stable}
                  are the cofibrations of the strict model stucture of prop.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects are precisely the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
            %p
              Moreover, this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#CofibrantlyGeneratedModelCategory"}> def.
              ) with generating (acyclic) cofibrations the sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^{stable}
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              ) from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#May02"}> Mandell-May 02, theorem 4.2
            )
          %p
            We give the
            %strong proof
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#StableModelStructureOnDiagramSpectraProof"} below
          %h5#proof_of_the_model_structure Proof of the model structure
          %p
            The generating cofibrations and acylic cofibrations are going to be the those induced via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
            of representables from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            (giving the strict model structure), together with an additional set of morphisms to the generating acylic cofibrations that will force fibrant objects to be Omega-spectra. To that end we need the following little preliminary.
          #ResolutionOfCorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps.num_defn
            %h6#definition_31 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_n
                    \\colon
                    F_{n+1}S^1
                    \\overset{k_n }{\longrightarrow}
                    Cyl(\lambda_n)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    F_n S^0
            %p
              be the factorization as in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              of the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_n
              of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingOfAdjunctsOfStructureMapsExists"}
              through its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ConeAndMappingCylinder"}> prop.
              ) formed with respect to the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+spectrum"} cylinder spectrum
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F_{n+1}S^1) \wedge (I_+)
          %p Notice that:
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_14 Lemma
            %p
              The factorization in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ResolutionOfCorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps"}
              is through a cofibration followed followed by a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})_{strict}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_49 Proof
            %p
              Since the cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              is cofibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{n+1}(-)
              is a left Quillen functor by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionSpectrumStructuredStrictQuillenAdjunction"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{n+1}S^1
              is cofibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi dia
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi strict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})_{strict}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardReducedCylinderOnStructuredSpectrumIsGood"}
              says that its standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+spectrum"} cylinder spectrum
              is a good
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              and then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FactorizationLemma"}> lemma
              ) says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              is a cofibration. Moreover, the morphism out of the standard mapping cylinder is a homotopy equivalence, with homotopies induced under tensoring from the standard homotopy contracting the standard cylinder.
          %p With this we may state the classes of morphisms that are going to be shown to be the classes of generating (acyclic) cofibrations for the stable model structures:
          #StableGeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_32 Definition
            %p
              Recall the sets of generating (acyclic) cofibrations of the strict model structre def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I^{stable}_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    I^{strict}_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J^{stable}_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    J^{strict}_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})}
                    \\;\sqcup\;
                    \\{
                    k_n \Box i_+
                    \\}_{{n \in \mathbb{N}} \atop {i \in I}}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of the strict acyclic generating cofibration with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+products"} pushout products
              under smash tensoring of the resolved maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ResolutionOfCorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps"}
              with the elements in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, def.6.2, def. 9.3
            )
          #ElementsOfKAreStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_15 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Dia
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi cg
                        %mo ,
                        %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Orth
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Seq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia \in \{Top^{\ast/}_{cg,fin}, Orth, Seq\}
              (but not
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sym
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J^{stable}_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod(Top_{cg})}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableGeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a cofibration with respect to the strict model structure (prop.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stable weak homotopy equivalence
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_50 Proof
            %p First regarding strict cofibrations:
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against the strict fibrations, hence in particular they are strict cofibrations. Moreover, by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal-Tierney+calculus"} Joyal-Tierney calculus
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#JoyalTierneyCalculus"}> prop.
              ),
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              has left lifting against any acyclic strict fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              has left lifting against
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo □
                          %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{\Box i}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutProductWithRespectToSmashTensoringSatisfiesEnrichedModelCategoryAxioms"}
              the latter is still a strict acyclic fibration. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              by construction is a strict cofibration, the lifting follows and hence also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is a strict cofibration.
            %p Now regarding stable weak homotopy equivalences:
            %p
              The morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{strict}
              by design are strict weak equivalences, hence they are in particular stable weak homotopy equivalences. The morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              are stable weak homotopy equivalences by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctsOfFreeSpectrumInclusionsAreOrAreNotStableWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
              and by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
            %p
              To see that also the pushout products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box (i_n)_+
              are stable weak homotopy equivalences. (e.g.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#May02"} Mandell-May 02, p.46
            %p
              First
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \wedge (S^{n-1})_+
              is still a stable weak homotopy equivalence, by lemma.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmashTensoringWithFiniteCellComplexPreservesSWHE"}
            %p
              Moreover, observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dom(k_n)\wedge i_+
              is degreewise a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusion, hence degreewise a cofibration in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#S0FreeSpectraCellDegreewise"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dom(k_n) \wedge i_+
              is degreewise the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complex"} CW complex
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_+
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen} \longrightarrow (Top^{\ast/}_{cg})_{Quillen}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomProductAdjunctionForCofibrantObjectInPointedTopCGIsQuillen"}> prop.
              ) and hence preserves cofibrations.
            %p
              Altogether this implies by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutOfSWHEAlongDegreewiseCofibration"}
              that the pushout of the stable weak homotopy equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \wedge (S^{n-1})_+
              along the degreewise cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dom(k_n)\wedge i_+
              is still a stable weak homtopy equivalence, and so the pushout product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is, too, by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
          %p
            The point of the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            is to make the following true:
          #KInjectivesAreAcyclicCofibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_16 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              from def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableGeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p it is a fibration in the strict model structure (hence degreewise a fibration);
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
                  of structure map compatibility on the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mover
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mtd
                                %mi Ω
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mover
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mtd
                                %mi Ω
                                %msub
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        X_n  &amp;\overset{\tilde\sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega X_{n+1}
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        Y_n &amp;\underset{\tilde \sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega Y_{n+1}
                        }
                %p
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
                  (
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyPullback"}> def.
                  ).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 9.5
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_51 Proof
            %p
              By prop
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfStrictModelStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{strict}
              alone characterizes strict fibrations, hence degreewise fibrations. Lifting against the remaining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal-Tierney+calculus"} Joyal-Tierney calculus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_+
              against the dual pullback product of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo □
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{\Box k_n}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{\Box k_n}
              is a weak homotopy equivalence. But by construction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              and by lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingOfAdjunctsOfStructureMapsExists"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{\Box k_n}
              is the comparison morphism into the homotopy pullback under consideration.
          #KInjectivesObjectsAreOmegaSpectra.num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
          #KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_17 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
              which is both
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a stable weak homotopy equivalence (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi J
                            %mi stable
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
            %p
              is an acyclic fibration in the strict model structure of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              of topological spaces;
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, corollary 9.8
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_52 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to B
              be both a stable weak homotopy equivalence as well as a
              = succeed "-injective" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              contains, by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfStrictModelStructure"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is in particular a strict fibration, hence a degreewise fibration. Therefore the fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              in the strict model structure.
            %p
              Hence by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegreewiseLESofHomotopyGroupsInducedStableLES"}
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_{\bullet+1}(X)
                    \\overset{\pi_{\bullet+1}(f)}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_{\bullet+1}(Y)
                    \\overset{}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(F)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\pi_\bullet(X)
                    \\overset{\pi_\bullet(f)}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(Y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By exactness and by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(f)
              is an isomorphism, this implies that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(F) \simeq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to \ast
              is a stable weak homotopy equivalence.
            %p
              Observe also that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "-injective" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "injective+or+projective+morphism#ClosureProperties"} closure properties
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective object
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesObjectsAreOmegaSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is an Omega-spectrum. Since stable weak homotopy equivalences between Omega-spectra are already degreewise weak homotopy equivalences, together this says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \ast
              is a weak equivalence in the strict model structure, hence degreewise a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{\bullet \geq 1}(f_n)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and for each homotopy group in positive degree.
            %p
              To deduce the remaining case that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f_0)
              is an isomorphism, observe that, by assumption of
              = succeed "-injectivity," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesAreAcyclicCofibrations"}
              gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n
              is a homotopy pullback (in topological spaces) of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega (f_{n+1})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega (f_{n+1})
              is a weak homotopy equivalence, since
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(\Omega(-)) = \pi_{\bullet+1}(-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n
              is the homotopy pullback of a weak homotopy equivalence and hence itself a weak homotopy equivalence.
          #RetractsOfRelativeKCellComplexesAreTheStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_18 Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              are precisely the morphisms which are
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  stable weak homotopy equivalences (def.
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
              %li
                %p
                  as well as cofibrations with respect to the strict model structure of prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 9.9 (i)
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_53 Proof
            %p
              Since all elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              are stable weak homotopy equivalences as well as strict cofibrations by lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ElementsOfKAreStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations"}
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              In the other direction, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a stable weak homotopy equivalence and a strict cofibration, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              it factors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon \stackrel{i}{\to}\stackrel{p}{\to}
              as a relative
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              followed by a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a stable weak homotopy equivalence, and so by assumption and by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences"}
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a strict acyclic fibration. But then the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a strict cofibration means that it has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+lifting+property"} left lifting property
              against
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract+argument"} retract argument
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a retract of the relative
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          #KInjectivesAreIndeedTheStableFibrations.num_cor
            %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
              are precisely those which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective
              with respect to the cofibrations of the strict model structure that are also stable weak homotopy equivalences.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 9.9 (ii)
            )
          #StableAcyclicFibrationsAreEquivalentlyStrictAcyclicFibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_19 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
              (for
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Diq
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi Sym
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diq \neq Sym
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a stable weak homotopy equivalence (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective
                  with respect to the cofibrations of the strict model structure that are also stable weak homotopy equivalences;
            %p
              precisely if it is an acylic fibration in the strict model structure of theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 9.9 (iii)
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_54 Proof
            %p Every acyclic fibration in the strict model structure is injective with respect to strict cofibrations by the strict model structure; and it is a clearly a stable weak homotopy equivalence.
            %p
              Conversely, a morphism injective with respect to strict cofibrations that are stable weak homotopy equivalences is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
              by corollary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesAreIndeedTheStableFibrations"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences"}
              it is a strict acylic fibration.
          #StableModelStructureOnDiagramSpectraProof.proof
            %h6#proof_55 Proof
            %p
              (of theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalSpectraStableModelStructure"}
            %p
              The non-trivial points to check are the two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi stable
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi weq
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi fib
                      %mi stable
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cof_{stable}\cap weq_{stable} \;,\; fib_{stable})
              is a weak factorization system follows from lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfRelativeKCellComplexesAreTheStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations"}
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableAcyclicFibrationsAreEquivalentlyStrictAcyclicFibrations"}
              the stable acyclic fibrations are equivalently the strict acyclic fibrations and hence the weak factorization system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi fib
                      %mi stable
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi we
                      %mi stable
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cof_{stable} \;,\; fib_{stable} \cap we_{stable})
              is identified with that of the strict model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi cof
                        %mi strict
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi fib
                        %mi strict
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi we
                        %mi strict
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cof_{strict} \;,\; fib_{strict} \cap we_{strict})
          %h5#stability_of_the_homotopy_theory Stability of the homotopy theory
          %p
            We show now that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi OrthSpec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cg
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi stable
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OrthSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable}
            from theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalSpectraStableModelStructure"}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenEquivalence"}> def.
            ) to the stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SeqSpec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cg
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi stable
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable}
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableModelStructureOnSequentialSpectraIsModelCategory"}> thm.
            ), hence that they model the same
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          #SequentialSpectraQuillenEquivalence.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunction"} free-forgetful adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (seq_! \dashv seq^\ast)
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
              and theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenEquivalence"}> def.
              ) between the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StableModelStructureOnSequentialSpectraIsModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) and the stable model structure on orthogonal spectra from theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrthogonalSpectraStableModelStructure"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Quillen
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi seq
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi seq
                            %mo !
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    OrthSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{seq^\ast}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{seq_!}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq_{Quillen}}
                    SeqSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, theorem 10.4
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_56 Proof
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast
              “creates weak equivalences”, in that a morphism of orthogonal spectra is a weak equivalence precisely if the underlying morphism of sequential spectra is (by def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableOrthStructureClassesOfMorphisms"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#InCaseTheRightAdjointCreatesWeakEquivalences"} this prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X
                    \\longrightarrow
                    seq^\ast seq_! X
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stable weak homotopy equivalence
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrant generation
              of the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#AlternativeStableModelStructureOnSequentialSpectraIsModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) every cofibrant sequential spectrum is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi I
                        %mi seq
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{seq}^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForSeqSpecStable"}> def.
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopologicalCellComplex"} def.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi I
                      %mi seq
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                      %msubsup
                        %mi S
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi n
                                %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi n
                                %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                      %msubsup
                        %mi D
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I^{stable}_{seq}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    F_{n_1} S^{n_2-1}_+
                    \\overset{F_{n_1} (i_{n_2})_+ }{\longrightarrow}
                    F_{n_1} D^{n_2}_+
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq_!
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast
              both preserve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast
              because it evaluates at objects and colimits in the diagram category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi OrthSpec
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} OrthSpec
              are computed objectwise, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq_!
              because it is a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i X_i
              a relative
              = succeed "-decompositon" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi I
                        %mi seq
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^{stable}_{seq}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X \colon X \to seq^\ast seq_! X
              is equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i \eta_{X_i}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i X_i
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i seq_! seq^\ast X_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now observe that the colimits involved in a relative
              = succeed "-complex" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi I
                        %mi seq
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^{stable}_{seq}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+compositions"} transfinite compositions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LeftDerivedFunctorOfColimitFunctor"}> def.
              ): First, all objects involved are cofibrant. Now for the transfinite composition all the morphisms involved are cofibrations, so that their colimit is a homotopy colimit by
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ProjectiveModelStructureOnNSequencesOfTopologicalSpaces"} this example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
              by (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyPullback"}> def.
              ).
            %p
              It follows that if all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{X_i}
              are weak equivalences, then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta = \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i \eta_{X_i}
            %p Unwinding this, one finds that it is sufficient to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta_{F_{n_1} S^{n_2}}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    F_{n_1} S^{n_2}_+
                    \\longrightarrow
                    seq^\ast seq_! F_{n_1} S^{n_2}
            %p
              is a stable weak homotopy equivalence for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_1, n_2 \in \mathbb{N}
            %p
              Consider this for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≥
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_2 \geq n_2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_{n_1} S^{n_2} \longrightarrow F_{0} S^{n_2-n_1}
            %p
              whose components in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≥
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \geq n_1
              are the identity. These are the composites of the maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_k \wedge S^{k+n_2-n_1}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n_1
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_n
              from def. \reg{CorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps}. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctsOfFreeSpectrumInclusionsAreOrAreNotStableWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
              also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi seq
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi seq
                      %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast seq_! \lambda_n
              are weak homotopy equivalences. Hence we have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagrams"} commuting diagrams
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                              %mi seq
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mn 0
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi η
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi seq
                              %mo *
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                              %mi orth
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi seq
                              %mo *
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mn 0
                              %mi orth
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo −
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    F^{seq}_{n_1} S^{n_2} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; F_0 S^{n_2-n_1}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\eta}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    seq^\ast F^{orth}_{n_1}S^{n_2-n_1}
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    seq^\ast F_0^{orth} S^{n_2-n_1}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the horizontal maps are stable weak homotopy equivalences by the previous argument and the right vertical morphism is an isomorphism by the formula in prop.
              = succeed ".Hence" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitFormOfFreeSpectra"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_2 \lt n_1
              then one reduces this to the above case by smashing with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n_1-n_2}
          #StableHomotopyCategoryStructuredSpectra.num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              Theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectraQuillenEquivalence"}
              means that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
