            %p
              Therefore in this case we have an isomorphism for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              For general
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is represented by a sequential
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectrum"} CW-spectrum
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#CWApproximationForSequentialSpectra"}> prop.
              ). Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibers"} homotopy cofibers
              of its cell attachment maps are suspensions of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StrictModelStructureCellAttachmentToSpectra"}> rmk.
              ).
            %p
              First consider the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a CW-spectrum with finitely many cells. Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber+sequence"} homotopy cofiber sequence
              of the
              = succeed "st" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
