          %h2#references References
          %p
            The model structure on orthogonal spectra and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sequential+spectra"} model structure on sequential spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+excisive+functors"} model structure on excisive functors
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#MMSS00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"} Stefan Schwede
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+categories+of+diagram+spectra"} Model categories of diagram spectra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/mmssLMSDec30.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://plms.oxfordjournals.org/content/82/2/441.short?rss=1&ssource=mfc"} publisher
          %blockquote
            %p#CaveatOnDefinitionOfStableWeakEquivalences
              Caveat. In (
              %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00
              ) the weak equivalences of the stable model structure are first defined to be the “stable equivalences”, then the proof of the model structure is given in terms of these, and afterwards it is shown that for orthogonal spectra the “stable equivalences” coincide with the stable weak homotopy equivalences (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet
              \-isomorphisms) that we use here. This approach makes the proof of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences"}
              involve a certain detour (for the step where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to\ast
              is concluded to be a weak equivalence, see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+categories+of+diagram+spectra"} Model categories of diagram spectra
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Model+categories+of+diagram+spectra#WhyFIsStablyEquivalentToThePoint"} here
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#May02"} Mandell-May 02
              = succeed "-isomorphisms)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#MMSS00"} MMSS 00
              %a{:href => "#MonoidalStableModelStructure"} above
              discussion means to give.
          %p
