          %p
            The analogous result for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
            is in
          %ul
            %li#May02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant orthogonal spectra and S-modules
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0408/MMM.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
          %ul
            %li
              Martin Stolz, around prop. 1.3.10 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant Structure on Smash Powers of Commutative Ring Spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/mstolz.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relevant theory of monoids in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
            is due to
          %ul
